Subject: iOS menus: a finger's click lands where the focus walk says it is

Online round 2 (D-105). D-083's menuIosPointOnFocusedItem() (overlay 0051)
swallows a touch click that is not on the focused item, by walking the dialog's
columns and rows the way dialogChangeItemFocusWithMouse() does. Upstream has
since widened the focus walk's last column out to the dialog's side ("the online
pages' windows are wider than their columns"), and the iOS copy kept the
column's own width. On Create Room the centred Create row's focus came from the
wide walk, the click test then said "not on the focused item", and the row lit
up but could never be pressed by touch (a pad's A pressed it). Same pick width
in both now.

Entirely inside PLATFORM_IOS.

--- a/src/game/menu.c
+++ b/src/game/menu.c
@@ -1661,8 +1661,22 @@
 
 	for (col = 0; col < dialog->numcols; col++, curx += colwidth) {
 		s32 colindex = dialog->colstart + col;
+		s32 pickwidth;
 		colwidth = menu->cols[colindex].width;
-		if (mx <= curx || mx >= curx + colwidth) {
+		pickwidth = colwidth;
+
+		// The same pick width dialogChangeItemFocusWithMouse() uses (overlay
+		// 0061): the last column reaches the dialog's side, as upstream draws
+		// it for the online pages' windows. Without it the focus walk took a
+		// finger on a row's right half (Create Room's Create, centred in a
+		// window wider than its column) and this test then called the same
+		// point "not on the focused item" and swallowed the click: the row
+		// lit up and could never be pressed by touch.
+		if (col == dialog->numcols - 1 && curx + colwidth < dialog->x + dialog->width - 2) {
+			pickwidth = dialog->x + dialog->width - 2 - curx;
+		}
+
+		if (mx <= curx || mx >= curx + pickwidth) {
 			continue;
 		}
 
